 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393318 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393318 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "335c8f2c-6e1a-56c3-b0b9-94d13c9ad70f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393319 #edb/ref 1080 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393319 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393319 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e6a6bdb-d757-58d4-980e-64a7fa142831" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393355 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393355 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73750" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393355 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393355 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=4 \\\\ -3x+6y=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393355 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "79d64547-fc54-5cd3-a6ec-b00c0e085729" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393355 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=4 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=4.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4+2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393356 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393356 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393356 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393356 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393356 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393356 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393356 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393356 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186393357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393356 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6afd3c5a-4cfe-5522-860c-2a976e4f7487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393357 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393357 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393357 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "61158912-48df-568f-b8c6-401043de3356" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393358 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393358 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393358 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b67e4f3e-f87e-52c3-931c-19e41ea8804e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393359 #edb/ref 1080 "No solution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393359 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393359 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "daca8fd6-ddfa-58d2-b860-3aa870c088ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393360 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393360 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393360 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fd3e4855-2511-5dd7-a436-6356b9877af3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393361 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393361 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393361 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "38bce7da-e628-523d-8d9f-797bcb20aca4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393877 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393877 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78549" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393877 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393877 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+4z=-2 \\\\ x+3y+9z=0 \\\\ y+6z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393877 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c98c808b-049b-59b0-8d36-61df2339933c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393877 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=0,y=-3,z=1.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=0+(-3)+1=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393878 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393878 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393878 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393878 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393878 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393878 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393878 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393878 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186393883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393878 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4352c172-b7da-52e6-b834-2727aa018a4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393879 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393879 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393879 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4e5fd665-92c8-5de9-a962-94e1f5665e2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393880 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393880 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393880 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b49b5346-149e-5688-b4e3-abd91ac82b0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393881 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393881 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393881 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dde44d62-1c85-5ae3-b2b1-d15a071a6e4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393882 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393882 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393882 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "86f61021-d77c-54